WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
Here are two materials made
of exactly the same thing:

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.450
carbon atoms, and nothing else.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.950
One is diamond.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.670
It is very hard, and it will
not conduct electricity.

5
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.110
The other is graphite, the
grey stuff in your pencil.

6
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.770
It is soft, it feels slippery,
and it does conduct electricity.

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.970
Same atoms, completely
different behaviour.

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.470
So how can that be?

9
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.830
In this mission, you'll compare
the giant structures of diamond

10
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.600
and graphite, and count the
bonds each carbon atom makes.

11
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.770
You'll meet graphene, a
sheet just one atom thick.

12
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.790
And you'll see how
metals hold together,

13
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.270
and why alloys are harder.

14
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.190
Your mission: explain how the
same atoms make such different

15
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.540
materials.
